Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; ============================================================================
;  Raise the GPU timeout window for long diffusion sampling (H3 on Arc B70)
; ============================================================================
;  WHY: UR_RESULT_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST (error 20) at SamplerCustomAdvanced.
;  Intel Arc has no memory-efficient SDPA kernel, so ComfyUI's standard
;  attention falls back to the math backend, whose giant attention kernels
;  can block the GPU for minutes. TdrLevel=3 + TdrDelay=60 declares a hang
;  and resets the driver mid-step, which Level Zero surfaces as DEVICE_LOST
;  and kills the generation.
;
;  WHAT THIS SETS:
;    TdrLevel = 3      keep hang detection ON (TdrLevel=0 caused 38 Event-41
;                      full-machine crashes on this machine — do not disable)
;    TdrDelay = 600    wait 10 minutes before declaring a hang
;    TdrDdiDelay = 600 same window at the DDI watchdog level
;
;  TRADEOFF: a genuine GPU wedge freezes the machine for up to 10 minutes
;  before TDR recovers it, and a tripped generation is still lost. That is
;  the accepted cost of multi-minute sampling kernels on a 33B DiT.
;
;  REQUIRES A REBOOT to take effect.
;  To undo, run tdr-enable-recovery.reg (also in this folder).
; ============================================================================

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\GraphicsDrivers]
"TdrLevel"=dword:00000003
"TdrDelay"=dword:00000258
"TdrDdiDelay"=dword:00000258
